    "reason": "SDK module names are namespaced. WikiWorkspace provides a read-only identity preflight and accepts validateSourceAccess for source operations; CoordinatedFiles checks that callback immediately before its existing revision CAS/publication. WikiWorkspace.localSearchPage retains source/epoch validation without constructing Spotlight; existing WikiSearchService delegates its local page method. Default callbacks preserve application callers. Frontmatter validation, ontology declarations and source-line coordinates are separated by responsibility; source newline/body preparation shares one implementation without changing parser or public contracts. Workspace scanning and write-result types are separated from the source mutation actor; the existing POSIX error factory is shared. Actor admission, publication and recovery ordering are preserved. Spotlight indexing, delegate callbacks and search orchestration now have separate source files; recovery and delegate share the same one-shot acknowledgement bridge. iOS Spotlight queries use the same host-selected data-protection class as their searchable index. Search candidates use one retained provider slot with bounded waiting and cancellation; source admission is rechecked after provider waits. Evidence verification exposes per-reference source checks without asserting truth or answerability. Semantic search accepts an injected multilingual retrieval embedding, uses raw source sections and purpose-specific revision-bound vector caches, rejects weak candidates and removes obsolete semantic vectors. Relations prefilter eligible targets before symmetric similarity. Policy version 3 invalidates obsolete unexecuted proposals while committed/uncertain operations remain receipt-driven. Source-scoped durable proposals and exact-plan approval use the existing writer and receipts. Internal filter validation and producer-namespace cache cleanup are package-scoped. Retrieval now requires a separate joint query/passage relevance provider; absent or invalid relevance never falls back to unchecked dense hits. Epoch validation follows both model stages. Optional relevance fields preserve old Codable reports. Idle resource release is deferred during searches and leaves sources, vectors, proposals and receipts intact. Knowledge queries index admitted Markdown and linked text PDFs in persistent transactional blocks, re-extract current PDF quotations, retain source scope and coverage, and reuse the optional embedding/relevance providers across the whole corpus. Saved knowledge-note markers prevent derived quotations becoming primary evidence. Attachment completion observes an existing receipt and rechecks original asset/note hashes without replaying a source effect. Knowledge retrieval shares the reranker candidate bound, validates exact UTF-8 and batched PDF anchors, and binds app cloud evidence to the admitted account. Knowledge-note publication rechecks source after writer refresh. Attachment copy observation retains the operation ID and distinguishes an absent ledger from an unreadable one. Saved PDF citation links reopen the recorded page only after the note revision and evidence are verified against current admitted source. The in-place Markdown preview returns the same validated source revision as the selected evidence. Managed local iOS evidence can bind to a persisted installation and workspace identity across container relocation. Attachment previews use content-addressed copies with the display filename. Saved Markdown citations reuse current source verification and reopen the recorded section. Knowledge inventory excludes the exact generated PDF companion as a primary Markdown source while admitting its linked PDF. Image-only PDF pages use bounded on-device Vision OCR. Positioned PDF text supports localized layout groups; saved and live regions re-extract against current PDF bytes while legacy PDFKit citations retain their original identity. Mixed PDF pages scan actual painted image placements, recognize only those visible crops and deduplicate overlapping native text. Regional citation validation reprocesses only the cited image. Markdown links use shared encoding and distinguish colons inside relative filenames from URL schemes.",
